    "body": "Merged main to resolve conflicts. The conflict tick stopped on these, but both sides compose rather than clash.\n\n- **Posts, opening comment (fanuc, fanuc-lathe, haas, mazak, sinumerik, tormach):** this PR states the document's program comment, and main's #594 cleans the machine name. The resolution takes the program comment first (`progComment()` is already cleaned), else `clean(nm)`, else `CAMCRAFT`.\n  - Fanuc, fanuc-lathe, Haas and Mazak keep this PR's O-word.\n  - Sinumerik keeps this PR's MPF header and `PROGRAM n - …` line.\n  - Tormach's `headTitle` now cleans the name and goes through main's `note()`.\n- **`posting.rs` modules, `mcp_setup.rs` gate map and tests:** keep both.\n\nTargeted gate:\n- app: lib 103, `mcp_setup` 3, `conformance` 6, `fanuc_post` 11, `posting` 23, `golden_cl` 4, `tormach_post` 7, `comment_escape` 5, `program_comments` 17, `lathe_post` 13, `probe_dialects` 7, `probe_tormach` 4, `heidenhain_block_form` 9, `program_entry` 9, `project_roundtrip` 71, `tormach_machines` 3, and the safe-retract suites: all green.\n- `camcraft-post` is all green.\n- clippy `-D warnings` on the app lib + `mcp_setup`: clean.\n\nStill a draft: it changes posted G-code, so it waits on a Hub run. Ready for a re-check (/resolve-conflicts check).",
